#~ shadowed_header
# fixedbugs, defect 2344 (panel 237's R2): `C_INCLUDE_PATH` names a folder
# holding a `stdbool.h` that defines `true` as 0, which clang searches before
# the platform's as a `-c-isystem` folder; `print(true)` printed `false` at
# exit 0. Refused at the program's first byte, its note naming the variable.

function main()
    b = true
    print(b)
